00:00:02.070 --> 00:00:04.150 align:start position:0%
as the delta variant holds its grip on  the nation and clark county the southern  nevada health district is opening new  testing kiosks around the valley hector  mejia live in the east side near eastern  the 95 explaining how the new testing  sites work  hector  well these kiosks are designed to limit  contact between staff and people who are  here to get a test once you're done with  the test you hand it over to someone  who's behind a plexiglas window at the  testing site right behind us and it all  happens outdoors we are at the east las  vegas community center by eastern and  the 95 but these kiosks are also at the  cambridge parkdale and walnut recreation  centers plus the alexander library and  this is bringing more options to people  in this neighborhood especially those  who are not able to make appointments  online it offers free testing to  walk-ups and people who set up an  appointment through the southern nevada  health district's website it'll stay  open for the next six to eight weeks  mondays through fridays from noon to 6  pm  councilwoman olivia diaz represents this  award she also sits on the board of the  southern nevada health district and she  recommends everyone to get tested even  if you are fully vaccinated if you start  to feel sick  there can be breakthrough cases and the  symptoms are milder so i would say out  of an abundance of caution if you're  feeling symptoms that feel like a flu  just come and get tested it may be  coveted and you just don't want to be a  carrier  according to the cdc's website the level  of covet transmission here in clark  county remains high the councilwoman  says the east side has been  disproportionately affected by the virus  this kiosk will help front line workers  who get exposed to positive cases and  need to get tested and now with the  schools open this is also going to help  those students who may get exposed while  they're in the classroom and need a  negative test before returning back to  class reporting on the east side hector  mejia 8 news now
 

